    },
    "live": {
      "wallet-multi": [
        "wallet-multi:primary:tx_123",
        "wallet-multi:secondary:tx_123"
      ]
    },
    "notes": "The forbidden-rule guard: provider_id 'tx_123' appears on TWO DIFFERENT SURFACES ('primary' and 'secondary') naming two UNRELATED events (100000 sat vs 200000 sat) -- a coincidence the fixture makes deliberate. A host that dedups by provider_id alone (spec/wire.md c: 'DEDUP BY provider_id ALONE IS FORBIDDEN') collapses these into one event, and expect.live -- DECLARED as two entries, not derived by folding this ledger -- says so. The correct key is local_id, which already encodes the surface.\n\nThe third history entry is wallet-multi:primary:tx_123 AGAIN, byte-identical: an idempotent provider re-send inside one page. The ledger is a SEQUENCE, so all three arrivals are declared in arrival order and the re-send is retained (A8) rather than collapsed -- while the live set still holds exactly one entry for that local_id, since both arrivals describe the same state. Sequence equality is also what makes the second-run id swap visible: swapping the two local_ids leaves the id SET, the counts and the live set all identical, and only the id-to-record association in this ordered sequence contradicts it (A9)."
  }
}
